<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<speak version="1.0" xml:lang="en-GB">
  <!-- AI CUE: TITLE: clear and composed; give the heading room. Do not perform as narrative prose. -->
  <p><s>Chapter 76: Seven</s></p><break time="700ms"/>
  <break time="1400ms"/>
  <!-- AI CUE: DIALOGUE: speak naturally; distinguish the speaker subtly using the wording and context. Do not invent an accent or emotion. -->
  <p>"Six," said Corvin, as the flame touched the next notch.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: ACTION: make the phrasing alert and precise; only raise pace or intensity slightly when the sentence supports it. Keep every word clear. -->
  <p>The dust came down out of the dome in a thin grey stream onto the carved stone between them. Small stones with it, pattering. Over their heads, through the rock, through the floor of the tower, the sound of Kharrak digging. Claws in stone. Closer. A second crack ran across the dome from the passage to the far wall.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>The men holding Calder looked up.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: DIALOGUE: speak naturally; distinguish the speaker subtly using the wording and context. Do not invent an accent or emotion. -->
  <p>"Five."</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>Below the ledge, out in the dark, the six chains groaned.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: REFLECTION: use measured, inward phrasing; keep emotion restrained and grounded in the text. -->
  <p>All of them at once. Going taut, the way they'd gone taut before, but further. Harder. A sound so deep it wasn't a sound, it was the rock round them shaking, and it didn't stop. It held. And held. Like a rope with a horse leaning back on it, a horse the size of a hill.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>The candle-flame on the floor beside the iron boss bent sideways and stood up again.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>The letters in the stone disc were brighter. Calder saw it under his own knees. The rings of them coming up white out of the grey, ring after ring, like coals coming up when you work the bellows, and not going down again.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>On the edge of the disc the grey man got to his feet.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: DIALOGUE: speak naturally; distinguish the speaker subtly using the wording and context. Do not invent an accent or emotion. -->
  <p>"Four," said Corvin.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>He hadn't moved. He knelt on the iron boss in the middle of the stone disc with his long pale hand on the bow of the key and his eyes on the candle, calm, as a man kneels at a wayside shrine. He didn't look up at the dome, or the dust, or Calder.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>Kharrak, said Calder. Kharrak, now, now, now…</p>
 <break time="1400ms"/>
  <!-- AI CUE: DIALOGUE: speak naturally; distinguish the speaker subtly using the wording and context. Do not invent an accent or emotion. -->
  <p>"Three."</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>The dome came in.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>The part over the passage, where the crack was. It came down in one great slab, rock and earth and stone, and the noise of it was louder than the river going out, and through the hole where it had been, out of the dark and the dust, came Kharrak.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: ACTION: make the phrasing alert and precise; only raise pace or intensity slightly when the sentence supports it. Keep every word clear. -->
  <p>Head first. Rust-red, filthy, bleeding from a long cut down his side, with his claws still out from the digging and the fire coming up in his throat. He came through the hole in the dome into the chamber with the floor of the tower coming down round him in pieces, and the light of his fire went over everything, white, and the men holding Calder let go.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: ACTION: make the phrasing alert and precise; only raise pace or intensity slightly when the sentence supports it. Keep every word clear. -->
  <p>They didn't decide to. They saw a dragon come through the roof and their hands opened.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: ACTION: make the phrasing alert and precise; only raise pace or intensity slightly when the sentence supports it. Keep every word clear. -->
  <p>The grey man didn't run. He planted his feet on the white letters and threw his hands up at Kharrak's head.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: ACTION: make the phrasing alert and precise; only raise pace or intensity slightly when the sentence supports it. Keep every word clear. -->
  <p>The weight hit Kharrak in the face. Calder felt it through the red mark, like a fist on his own nose. Kharrak's head went back and sideways and the fire in his throat went up into the broken dome instead of out, and he came down off the rubble onto his knees on the edge of the disc, shaking his head.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: ACTION: make the phrasing alert and precise; only raise pace or intensity slightly when the sentence supports it. Keep every word clear. -->
  <p>The grey man fell over. Straight down, like a coat dropped off a peg. Calder saw his face as he went, and his hair, and his hair had gone white from the roots, all of it, in a breath.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>Calder went for the key.</p>
 <break time="1400ms"/>
  <!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>He was a pace from it. He'd been a pace from it the whole time, with four men holding him. He went across the pace on his knees and got his hand on Corvin's wrist.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>Corvin looked at him.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>For the first time. Straight at him. Their faces a hand's breadth apart. Calder's hand on his wrist, round it, gripping, with everything he had.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: DIALOGUE: speak naturally; distinguish the speaker subtly using the wording and context. Do not invent an accent or emotion. -->
  <p>"Two," said Corvin.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: ACTION: make the phrasing alert and precise; only raise pace or intensity slightly when the sentence supports it. Keep every word clear. -->
  <p>He didn't pull against Calder's hand. He didn't try to shake it off. He knelt there with Calder holding his wrist, and looked at him with his grey eyes, and Calder pulled, and pulled, and the hand didn't move off the key. It was like pulling at a tree.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: REFLECTION: use measured, inward phrasing; keep emotion restrained and grounded in the text. -->
  <p>Not strength, Calder thought. He's not stronger than me. He's a thin man with a clerk's hands.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>He just won't.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>Kharrak…</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>Kharrak was in the chamber. Behind him. Rock still coming down. Calder felt him coming, felt the heat on his back, felt the red tide going up and over, felt Kharrak see the key and the hand and the wrist…</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: DIALOGUE: speak naturally; distinguish the speaker subtly using the wording and context. Do not invent an accent or emotion. -->
  <p>"One," said Corvin.</p>
 <break time="1400ms"/>
  <!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>He turned it.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: TENSION: use controlled, attentive phrasing and let pauses preserve suspense. Do not become theatrical. -->
  <p>With Calder's hand on his wrist. With Calder pulling back against him with all his weight. He turned the long black key in the iron boss, and it turned as if it wanted to, as if it had been waiting three hundred years to be turned and was glad.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>And the whole stone disc turned with it.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: REFLECTION: use measured, inward phrasing; keep emotion restrained and grounded in the text. -->
  <p>Calder felt it go under his knees. The great carved floor as wide as a threshing floor, grinding, turning, a quarter of a turn. The rings of letters cut in it sliding past each other. Ring past ring. The letters in each ring meeting the letters in the next, and stopping, in a line. A line of letters from the rim to the iron boss, all at once, where there'd been no line before.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>It lit. The whole line, white, rim to boss, so bright it came up through his knees and he saw the bones of his own hand round Corvin's wrist, dark inside the skin.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>The grinding stopped.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: TENSION: use controlled, attentive phrasing and let pauses preserve suspense. Do not become theatrical. -->
  <p>And in the same breath, a long way off, under the river, toward Greyhold, the same sound.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: TENSION: use controlled, attentive phrasing and let pauses preserve suspense. Do not become theatrical. -->
  <p>He felt it through his knees. Through the stone disc. Through the rock. Far off. So far off he couldn't tell if it was a sound or only the ground. A great slow grinding turn. The same. In the same breath. As if somewhere a long way away, under the other bank, under the school, another floor had turned under another hand at the same moment as this one.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>Two hands.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>Corvin felt it too. Calder saw him feel it. Kneeling on the iron boss with his hand on the key and Calder's hand on his wrist, he lifted his head, very slightly, listening.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>And he smiled.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>It was the only time Calder ever saw him do it. A small smile. Not like his brother's. Satisfied. The smile of a man at the weighing-post when the sack comes out at the weight he said.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>Then he let go of the key, and Calder's hand came away with nothing in it, and Corvin was up and walking across the lit stone to the rim as if he'd paced it out beforehand. Calder, held by the grinding in the stone, couldn't get up off his knees to follow.</p>
 <break time="1400ms"/>
  <!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>The seal opened.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: ACTION: make the phrasing alert and precise; only raise pace or intensity slightly when the sentence supports it. Keep every word clear. -->
  <p>He'd thought it would be a door. Something that swung, or slid, or lifted.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>The floor went. The stone disc dropped. All of it. Out from under him. Dropping, whole, like a trap-door, and he was on it, kneeling, and then there was nothing under his knees at all. And the chamber floor round it went too, the rock round the rim cracking away in a great ring and going down after it. The passage too, and the ledge beyond it. The grey man went down with the disc, lying where he'd fallen, and didn't move.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>And above.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: ACTION: make the phrasing alert and precise; only raise pace or intensity slightly when the sentence supports it. Keep every word clear. -->
  <p>He felt it above. Through the marks. The tower. The round room at its foot where Kharrak had dug through. The arch. The lion's long smooth hollow in the threshold. The verse over the arch, six lines, let no hand wake it. All of it, cracking, going down. The fort round it. The broken walls. The great fire in the middle of the fort, falling into the hole. The Old Ruin, that had stood on its island in the river since before there was a Hearthmere, since there was a bridge, falling into the dark under it all at once with a sound like the end of the world.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: ACTION: make the phrasing alert and precise; only raise pace or intensity slightly when the sentence supports it. Keep every word clear. -->
  <p>He fell.</p>
 <break time="1400ms"/>
  <!-- AI CUE: ACTION: make the phrasing alert and precise; only raise pace or intensity slightly when the sentence supports it. Keep every word clear. -->
  <p>He fell for a long time.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: ACTION: make the phrasing alert and precise; only raise pace or intensity slightly when the sentence supports it. Keep every word clear. -->
  <p>He didn't know which way was up. Rock falling round him, past him, with him. Dust. Darkness, and in the darkness, now and then, fire, Kharrak's, white, lighting the falling stone for a moment like a lantern swung in a mill. He heard Kharrak roar. Close. Then further. He felt Kharrak's wings jam in the falling rock and tear free and jam again.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: REFLECTION: use measured, inward phrasing; keep emotion restrained and grounded in the text. -->
  <p>He felt the ground of the cavern coming up at him out of the dark, a long way down. He couldn't see it. He knew it was there. The way you know the bottom of a well is there when you drop a stone.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: REFLECTION: use measured, inward phrasing; keep emotion restrained and grounded in the text. -->
  <p>I'm sorry, he thought. Wren. I'm sorry.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>Something came down through the falling rock above him.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: ACTION: make the phrasing alert and precise; only raise pace or intensity slightly when the sentence supports it. Keep every word clear. -->
  <p>Fast. Faster than the rock. Wings folded, head down, like a stone thrown at the bottom of the world. Bronze. Huge. With one gold eye and the ruin where the other had been, and blood all down the plates of her chest where the ironback's horn had been in her.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>He felt her come. Through the bronze mark. He felt her tear free of the ironback in the fort as the fort went in under her, and fold her wings, and dive into the hole after him.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>Her forefoot closed round him in the dark.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>Round his whole body, as his hand would close round an egg. Claws as long as his arm, curved over him like the bars of a cage. Holding.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>She couldn't stop.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>She opened her wings.</p>
 <break time="1400ms"/>
  <!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>He felt them open. He'd felt her wings open a thousand times, on the hill, in the sky over the Marches, over the river at midwinter. He'd never felt this.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: REFLECTION: use measured, inward phrasing; keep emotion restrained and grounded in the text. -->
  <p>She opened her wings in the cavern under the Old Ruin, in the dark, among the falling stone, the first wings that had ever opened in that air in all the years since there'd been a cavern. They caught. The air was there. More air than he'd thought, more dark, more room. A great dark, going on and on in every direction past where any light could reach. They caught the air and she turned, and the falling stone went past them, and she was flying.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: REFLECTION: use measured, inward phrasing; keep emotion restrained and grounded in the text. -->
  <p>Not well. Not long. She was hurt and heavy and the ironback's horn had been in her chest. She came down in a long slanting rush through the dark with the rock still falling round them, and the sound of it going on above, and her wings beating once, twice, three times, and then the ground.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: ACTION: make the phrasing alert and precise; only raise pace or intensity slightly when the sentence supports it. Keep every word clear. -->
  <p>A slope. Rubble. She hit it hard on her hind legs and her chest and slid, and he felt her forefoot keep him off the stones, curled round him, while she slid down the rubble on her bronze plates with a noise like a ploughshare on rock. A long way. Then she stopped.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>She lay there.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>He lay in her forefoot.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>The rock went on falling. Above them, behind them, out in the dark, the rest of the Old Ruin coming down. It went on and on. Then smaller. Then stones, one at a time, rattling down the slope. Then nothing.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>The dust settled.</p>
 <break time="1400ms"/>
  <!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>Calder, said Aurveth.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: DIALOGUE: speak naturally; distinguish the speaker subtly using the wording and context. Do not invent an accent or emotion. -->
  <p>"Yes."</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>Are you…</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: DIALOGUE: speak naturally; distinguish the speaker subtly using the wording and context. Do not invent an accent or emotion. -->
  <p>"Yes." He didn't know if he was. He moved his arms. His legs. Everything hurt. Everything moved. "Yes. Are you?"</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>She didn't answer.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: ACTION: make the phrasing alert and precise; only raise pace or intensity slightly when the sentence supports it. Keep every word clear. -->
  <p>He felt her through the bronze mark and he didn't need her to. The horn-wound in her chest, deep, pulsing. Her wings, the left one wrenched, the joint torn. Her back, the old scars from the mill opened again. She lay on the rubble with her great head down on the stones and her breath going in and out of her, slow, ragged, and he felt every bit of it.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: DIALOGUE: speak naturally; distinguish the speaker subtly using the wording and context. Do not invent an accent or emotion. -->
  <p>"Aurveth."</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>I'm here, she said. I've been here before. A long pause. Not here. But hurt like this. I'm old. I've been hurt like this.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>Her forefoot opened.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>He crawled out of it onto the rubble.</p>
 <break time="1400ms"/>
  <!-- AI CUE: ACTION: make the phrasing alert and precise; only raise pace or intensity slightly when the sentence supports it. Keep every word clear. -->
  <p>It was dark. Somewhere above, very far up, there was light: a ragged hole, orange, where the island had been, with fire still burning at the edges of it, a long way up. It didn't reach down here. It lit the dust hanging in the air above them, and the edges of things, and nothing else.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>Kharrak came down the slope.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>Out of the dark above them. Sliding, clawing, falling and catching himself, in a shower of loose stone, with his wings half open and jammed with rubble and his head down. He came down the slope of fallen rock onto the stones beside them and stopped, and stood there, swaying.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: ACTION: make the phrasing alert and precise; only raise pace or intensity slightly when the sentence supports it. Keep every word clear. -->
  <p>Cut. Burned. One horn broken off short. Blood running down his side from the ironback and from the rock and from the digging, and his claws torn. Alive.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>He put his head down to Calder.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>You're alive, said Kharrak.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: DIALOGUE: speak naturally; distinguish the speaker subtly using the wording and context. Do not invent an accent or emotion. -->
  <p>"Yes."</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>I felt you fall. The red tide was low. I couldn't reach you. I was in the rock.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: DIALOGUE: speak naturally; distinguish the speaker subtly using the wording and context. Do not invent an accent or emotion. -->
  <p>"She caught me."</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>Kharrak looked at Aurveth, lying on the stones.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>He lay down beside her, close, against her side, and put his head on her neck. She let him.</p>
 <break time="1400ms"/>
  <!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>He heard the ironback go past.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>Out in the dark below them. Something huge coming down the slope of rubble from above, not sliding, falling, end over end, plates and horn and the great humped back, and past them, close enough that the wind of it went over his face, and on, down, into a deeper dark below the slope.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: ACTION: make the phrasing alert and precise; only raise pace or intensity slightly when the sentence supports it. Keep every word clear. -->
  <p>It didn't make a sound when it hit.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>The man in grey who'd stood on its neck with his arm up didn't make one either.</p>
 <break time="1400ms"/>
  <!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>He looked for Corvin.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: ACTION: make the phrasing alert and precise; only raise pace or intensity slightly when the sentence supports it. Keep every word clear. -->
  <p>He couldn't see much. The dust. The dark. The fire very far up. But across the cavern, on the far side of the great hole the Old Ruin had fallen into, high up on the wall of the dark, there was a light.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>A lantern. Small. Yellow. Moving.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>Going up.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: TENSION: use controlled, attentive phrasing and let pauses preserve suspense. Do not become theatrical. -->
  <p>He watched it. It went up slowly, back and forth, back and forth. A stair he hadn't known was there. An older one. Cut into the far wall of the cavern, going up to somewhere he couldn't see. Three figures with it. One tall and thin, going first, not hurrying, not looking down.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>Corvin had known it was there. Of course he had. He'd read the verse. He'd read the cut pages, or the ones that hadn't been cut, or whatever the Restoration had that Hearthmere didn't. He'd known the floor would go. He'd knelt on the iron boss with his hand on the key and counted down to one and turned it, and when the floor went he'd already been at the edge of it, and the stair.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>The lantern went up the far wall and round a corner of the rock, and was gone.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: REFLECTION: use measured, inward phrasing; keep emotion restrained and grounded in the text. -->
  <p>He didn't look back once.</p>
 <break time="1400ms"/>
  <!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>Calder stood up on the rubble.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>He stood at the bottom of the slope of the fallen Ruin with the two dragons lying behind him, and looked out into the dark.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>There were the chains.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: ACTION: make the phrasing alert and precise; only raise pace or intensity slightly when the sentence supports it. Keep every word clear. -->
  <p>He could see them now. His eyes had found them. Going up past him into the dark above, toward the hole and the fire, where they'd been fixed to whatever had been above. Six. Black. Each link taller than a man. Taut. So taut they hummed. A deep note, all six together, that went through the rock and through his boots and through his teeth.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>And going down. Ahead of him. Into a deeper dark at the bottom of the cavern, further than the slope, further than anything. Down to where they were fastened to whatever they'd been fastened to for three hundred years.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>Something was moving down there.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>Not the dark moving, or water turning over. Something he couldn't see the edges of, that filled the deep dark at the bottom of the cavern, lifting, as a hill would lift if a hill could stand up.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>The chains groaned.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: ACTION: make the phrasing alert and precise; only raise pace or intensity slightly when the sentence supports it. Keep every word clear. -->
  <p>Up at the top of the slope, where the six chains went up into the dark toward the hole, there were stones. Great anchor-stones, set in the cavern wall, each as big as a house, with the chains running through iron eyes in them. He could see the nearest one in the light of the fire far above.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>It was cracking.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: TENSION: use controlled, attentive phrasing and let pauses preserve suspense. Do not become theatrical. -->
  <p>A long dark line running across the face of it, from the iron eye outward. Getting longer as he watched, like ice on a pond in the morning when somebody's walking out on it.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: REFLECTION: use measured, inward phrasing; keep emotion restrained and grounded in the text. -->
  <p>Two hands, he thought. Here and there. And it wakes.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>And it will not sleep again.</p>
 <break time="1400ms"/>
  <!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>He felt something.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: ACTION: make the phrasing alert and precise; only raise pace or intensity slightly when the sentence supports it. Keep every word clear. -->
  <p>Far off. Not from the hole where the Ruin had been, where the fire was. The other way. Across the cavern, through the rock, toward the far side of the river. Toward the Hearthmere bank. Toward Greyhold.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: ACTION: make the phrasing alert and precise; only raise pace or intensity slightly when the sentence supports it. Keep every word clear. -->
  <p>A small bright fire. Green. Frightened. Far off, under the other bank, and still.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>He stood on the rubble and stared into the dark toward it.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: QUESTION: shape the sentence as a genuine question, following its context; avoid an exaggerated upward lilt. -->
  <p>Lisska?</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>No answer. No words. Too far still, through too much rock. But the feeling. He'd know it anywhere. He'd felt it go west over the Brackenwood at first light with a bundle in her claw, going further and further until it was nearly nothing.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>Now it was there again. On the far side of the river, by the school. Still.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>He didn't understand it.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: REFLECTION: use measured, inward phrasing; keep emotion restrained and grounded in the text. -->
  <p>How? he thought. What's she doing at the school?</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>Beside it, so close to it he could hardly tell them apart, there was something else.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>Not his. He couldn't feel it the way he felt her. He felt it through her, the way he'd felt Morrow through Aurveth at the ford. Something very large, and very old, and warm, like the ground in summer. Somewhere under her, down in the dark.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: REFLECTION: use measured, inward phrasing; keep emotion restrained and grounded in the text. -->
  <p>With it, smaller, almost nothing, so faint he'd have missed it if Lisska hadn't been holding on to it the way she held on to him: somebody.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>A person.</p>
<break time="450ms"/></speak>
